1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
Most AI demos ask what an agent can do.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:08,973
Protocol Mirror asks a harder question:
what happens when models disagree on consequential evidence?

3
00:00:09,064 --> 00:00:13,400
We stress-tested 24 real clinical-trial
and publication pairs.

4
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:22,900
The page completed 48 out of 48 live WebMCP source reads,
returning 172 registry outcomes and 106 abstract sections.

5
00:00:22,991 --> 00:00:27,400
Then two local models received the same
blinded, exact-evidence task.

6
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:32,400
The 4-billion-parameter run called every decided
no-change case a change.

7
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:37,800
The 9-billion-parameter run missed 90.9 percent
of the decided change cases.

8
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:43,000
Those are run-specific grounding results,
not a universal hallucination or clinical-accuracy claim.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,365
Their opposite bias is the product argument.

10
00:00:45,457 --> 00:00:49,500
Protocol Mirror turns the page
into a typed evidence workspace.

11
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:59,749
The agent can inspect stable outcome identifiers, retrieve exact quotations,
stage a structured comparison, explain uncertainty, and move the right checkpoint into view.

12
00:00:59,840 --> 00:01:03,800
But there is no agent-callable
accept or reject action.

13
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:08,584
A human reviews both source spans and makes
the consequential decision here, in the interface.

14
00:01:08,676 --> 00:01:13,300
After that human decision, the capability surface
changes from six tools to seven.

15
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:19,200
The new receipt tool packages only reviewed work,
exact evidence locators, and the decision trail.

16
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:21,621
Staged suggestions stay out.

17
00:01:21,712 --> 00:01:25,500
The deterministic case keeps
the judging flow reliable.

18
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:34,498
Bounded live adapters bring current ClinicalTrials.gov and PubMed evidence
into the same visible workspace without silently turning it into a finding.

19
00:01:34,589 --> 00:01:38,500
Protocol Mirror is a research-transparency aid,
not medical advice,

20
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:42,922
a misconduct detector,
or a clinically validated decision system.

21
00:01:43,014 --> 00:01:46,600
The agent investigates, cites, proposes,
and packages proof.

22
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:50,046
The human remains accountable
for what the evidence means.

23
00:01:50,137 --> 00:01:53,288
AI assembles evidence. A human decides.
